# Static files and add-ons

- The static store lives in `uploads/static` (`utils.StaticDir`). HTTP CRUD is in `internal/handlers/static`, registered at `/build/static/{upload,list,delete,download}`.
- Store and serve files through `internal/utils`, preserving size limits and directory-containment checks.
- `docker.ValidateStaticAddons` / `ApplyStaticAddons` and `extract.ExtractStaticAddonIntoContext` unpack static-store ZIPs under a validated relative `extract_to` inside a Docker build context; `utils.CopyStaticFilesToDir` copies loose static files and skips selected add-on archives. This library has no HTTP caller yet; a future build pipeline will use it.
- Empty or `.` `extract_to` means the build-context root; root extraction stages entries and rejects collisions without deleting or overwriting existing files. Never trust archive entry paths. Nested archives are not expanded.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/extract/... ./internal/utils/... ./internal/docker/...`.
